WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:13.000
Leonardo: Come in, come in. Bernardo has 65 gold sheets for a new panel, and the panel must be 5 inches wide. How long will it be? A careful worker would know before cutting the wood. Would you? I'll watch.

00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:14.846
Here is the panel.

00:00:14.896 --> 00:00:16.538
We know two things.

00:00:16.588 --> 00:00:19.347
The area is 65 square inches.

00:00:19.397 --> 00:00:23.571
One side is 5 inches.

00:00:23.621 --> 00:00:26.423
The other side is missing.

00:00:26.473 --> 00:00:28.676
In what units is each one given?

00:00:28.726 --> 00:00:30.804
The area is in square inches.

00:00:30.854 --> 00:00:33.236
The side is in inches.

00:00:33.285 --> 00:00:36.009
They match, so we can start.

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:39.003
Each gold sheet covers 1 square inch.

00:00:39.053 --> 00:00:41.275
One row across the panel takes 5 sheets.

00:00:41.325 --> 00:00:42.878
Watch.

00:00:42.928 --> 00:00:43.770
One row: 5.

00:00:43.819 --> 00:00:45.041
Another row: 10.

00:00:45.091 --> 00:00:49.176
Keep going, row after row, all the way to 65.

00:00:49.226 --> 00:00:51.044
Now every sheet is used.

00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:52.201
How many rows did we make?

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:53.899
Let's count.

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:56.283
13 rows.

00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:59.055
Each row is 1 inch of the length.

00:00:59.105 --> 00:01:01.517
So the panel is 13 inches long.

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:05.232
Here is what we were really asking: 5 times what number makes 65?

00:01:05.282 --> 00:01:07.348
That is a missing factor.

00:01:07.398 --> 00:01:10.523
And we find a missing factor by dividing.

00:01:10.573 --> 00:01:13.725
65 divided by 5 is 13.

00:01:13.775 --> 00:01:15.939
Now check by multiplying.

00:01:15.989 --> 00:01:18.931
13 times 5 is 65.

00:01:18.981 --> 00:01:20.564
That is the area.

00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:22.267
It matches.

00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:23.953
Watch the unit.

00:01:24.003 --> 00:01:26.505
The area is in square inches.

00:01:26.555 --> 00:01:32.733
But the missing side is a length, so it is 13 inches, not 13 square inches.

00:01:32.783 --> 00:01:37.746
And if the side you know is in feet, change it to inches first.

00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:45.716
So, to find a missing side, ask: the side I know, times what, makes the area?

00:01:45.766 --> 00:01:48.848
Divide the area by the side you know.

00:01:48.898 --> 00:01:50.374
Then multiply to check.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:58.930
Leonardo: Thirteen inches. Bernardo can cut the wood now. But what if the side I knew were in feet? Your turn first. Try the panel below.
